.TH NEALS 1 "August 2026" "neals" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neals \- local platform orchestrator for devenv projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neals
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B neals
registers devenv projects, talks to the
.B nealsd
daemon over a UNIX socket, starts and stops projects in per-project network
namespaces, exposes HTTP routes at
.BI {service}.{project}.localhost
via Caddy, and provides a live log view plus a project shell in the same
namespace.
.PP
Requires
.B bubblewrap
and
.B slirp4netns
on the host.
.PP
With the systemd system unit installed, Caddy listens on
.B 127.0.0.1:80
so browser URLs need no port. In ad-hoc mode (daemon auto-started by the CLI)
Caddy listens on
.B 127.0.0.1:2015
and URLs must include that port.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B register
Register the current directory (reads
.B neals.name
from
.IR devenv.nix ).
.TP
.B list
List registered projects.
.TP
.BI unregister " name"
Remove a project from the registry.
.TP
.B prune
Remove registry entries whose paths no longer exist.
.TP
.BI up " name " [ \-d ]
Start a project. Opens a live view (routes + logs) unless
.B \-d
/
.B \-\-detach
is set. In the live view:
.BR Ctrl+C
or
.B q
detaches;
.B Ctrl+X
stops the project.
.TP
.BI down " name"
Stop a running project.
.TP
.B status
Show running projects, PIDs, and routes.
.TP
.BI logs " name " [ \-f ]
Print the last log lines;
.B \-f
opens the live view.
.TP
.BI bash " name"
Enter a quiet
.B devenv shell
in the project's network namespace (project must be
.BR up ).
Uses
.BR $SHELL .
bash/zsh get a short prompt
.BI neals: name\fR.
.TP
.BI exec " name \-\- command\&..."
Run a command inside the project netns and devenv.
.TP
.B doctor
Check tools, directories, HTTP bind, and daemon.
.TP
.B repl
Interactive command loop.
.TP
.BI completions " shell"
Print a one-line snippet to enable shell completion
(\fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, \fBfish\fR, \fBelvish\fR, \fBpowershell\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/neals/projects.json
Project registry.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/neals/
Project logs, Caddy config, shell rc snippets.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/neals/
Ad-hoc IPC socket and per-project runtime files.
.TP
.I /run/neals/nealsd.sock
System daemon IPC socket (when installed).
.TP
.I <project>/.neals/
Convenience symlinks to UNIX sockets (do not bind here).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NEALS_SOCKET
Override the IPC socket path.
.TP
.B NEALS_CADDY_HTTP_ADDR
Override Caddy listen address (e.g.
.BR 127.0.0.1:8080 ).
.TP
.B NEALS_MODE
Set to
.B system
by the systemd unit (default listen
.BR 127.0.0.1:80 ).
.TP
.B COMPLETE
Used internally for dynamic shell completion
(\fBCOMPLETE=bash neals\fR).
.PP
On
.BR up ,
each
.B neals.services.\fIsvc\fR.port
preferred port is fixed
.B inside
the netns and injected as
.BI NEALS_ SERVICE _PORT
(e.g.
.BR NEALS_REDIS_PORT ).
The host may get a different loopback port when the preferred one is busy;
.B status
shows host ports (and guest when they differ).
UNIX services also get
.BR NEALS_RUNTIME .
Legacy
.B neals.route.*=tcp
still works (ephemeral port + proxy) but is deprecated.
See the project README.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
neals register
neals up demo
neals status
neals bash demo
neals exec demo -- php artisan migrate
source <(COMPLETE=bash neals)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nealsd (8),
.BR devenv (1)
.PP
System install:
.I contrib/systemd/README.md
(after install:
.IR /usr/local/share/doc/neals/systemd.md ).
.SH AUTHORS
Neals contributors.
